W2 item 3a — is a mixed cell's mixedness LINEAR, and can the gauge fire on it?
  FIRES ⟺ keepMin is exactly one Aut-orbit ∧ the harvest is transitive on it.
  gauge <= Aut always ⟹ #gauge-orbits >= #Aut-orbits; EQUAL means the mixedness is
  entirely linear.  Every gauge element is verified edge-by-edge before use.

  CFI cubic m=8 pl  n=56  |E|=12  beta=dim(cycle space)=5  |gauge|=32
     base graph: |Aut(base)|=12, edge-orbit sizes [6, 3, 3]
     cell 0 (TARGET) [gadgets]: |cell|=32
        gauge-orbits: 8 sizes=[4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4]
        Aut-orbits  : 3 sizes=[12, 12, 8]
        ⟹ ⛔ NOT linear: Aut merges 8 gauge-orbits into 3 blocks
           the extra merging is BASE automorphism structure, which no linear
           solver supplies — so even a perfect key leaves 2+ reps
        ⟹ ⛔ NO Aut-block is a single gauge-orbit — every block splits into >= 2 gauge-orbits, so even a PERFECT key leaves >= 2 reps ⟹ THE CELL CANNOT FIRE on the gauge (block/gauge ratio 4)
     cell 1 [wires]: |cell|=24
        gauge-orbits: 12 sizes=[2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2]
        Aut-orbits  : 3 sizes=[12, 6, 6]
        ⟹ ⛔ NOT linear: Aut merges 12 gauge-orbits into 3 blocks
           the extra merging is BASE automorphism structure, which no linear
           solver supplies — so even a perfect key leaves 3+ reps
        ⟹ ⛔ NO Aut-block is a single gauge-orbit — every block splits into >= 3 gauge-orbits, so even a PERFECT key leaves >= 2 reps ⟹ THE CELL CANNOT FIRE on the gauge (block/gauge ratio 2)

  CFI cubic m=8 tw  n=56  |E|=12  beta=dim(cycle space)=5  |gauge|=32
     base graph: |Aut(base)|=12, edge-orbit sizes [6, 3, 3]
