        ⟹ ⛔ NO Aut-block is a single gauge-orbit — every block splits into >= 3 gauge-orbits, so even a PERFECT key leaves >= 2 reps ⟹ THE CELL CANNOT FIRE on the gauge (block/gauge ratio 2)

=== a SYMMETRIC base — removes the base's own asymmetry from the picture ===
  CFI over K4  n=28  |E|=6  beta=dim(cycle space)=3  |gauge|=8
     base graph: |Aut(base)|=24, edge-orbit sizes [6]
     cell 0 (TARGET) [gadgets]: |cell|=16
        gauge-orbits: 4 sizes=[4, 4, 4, 4]
        Aut-orbits  : 1 sizes=[16]
        ⟹ ⛔ NOT linear: Aut merges 4 gauge-orbits into 1 blocks
           the extra merging is BASE automorphism structure, which no linear
           solver supplies — so even a perfect key leaves 4+ reps
        ⟹ ⛔ NO Aut-block is a single gauge-orbit — every block splits into >= 4 gauge-orbits, so even a PERFECT key leaves >= 2 reps ⟹ THE CELL CANNOT FIRE on the gauge (block/gauge ratio 4)
     cell 1 [wires]: |cell|=12
        gauge-orbits: 6 sizes=[2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2]
        Aut-orbits  : 1 sizes=[12]
        ⟹ ⛔ NOT linear: Aut merges 6 gauge-orbits into 1 blocks
           the extra merging is BASE automorphism structure, which no linear
           solver supplies — so even a perfect key leaves 6+ reps
        ⟹ ⛔ NO Aut-block is a single gauge-orbit — every block splits into >= 6 gauge-orbits, so even a PERFECT key leaves >= 2 reps ⟹ THE CELL CANNOT FIRE on the gauge (block/gauge ratio 2)

  CFI over C6  n=24  |E|=6  beta=dim(cycle space)=1  |gauge|=2
     base graph: |Aut(base)|=12, edge-orbit sizes [6]
     cell 0 (TARGET) [gadgets]: |cell|=24
        gauge-orbits: 12 sizes=[2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2]
        Aut-orbits  : 1 sizes=[24]
        ⟹ ⛔ NOT linear: Aut merges 12 gauge-orbits into 1 blocks
           the extra merging is BASE automorphism structure, which no linear
           solver supplies — so even a perfect key leaves 12+ reps
        ⟹ ⛔ NO Aut-block is a single gauge-orbit — every block splits into >= 12 gauge-orbits, so even a PERFECT key leaves >= 2 reps ⟹ THE CELL CANNOT FIRE on the gauge (block/gauge ratio 2)

